  "result": "Perfect! All 281 tests pass. I've successfully implemented customer merge functionality:\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId)** in src/customers.js that:\n   - Normalizes both customer IDs\n   - Validates both customers exist (CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND)\n   - Prevents merging a customer with itself (SAME_CUSTOMER)\n   - Removes the `fromId` customer from the customers array\n   - Reassigns all invoices from `fromId` to `intoId` (handles non-normalized invoice IDs)\n   - Returns ok({ customers, invoices })\n   - Never mutates arguments, returns new arrays/objects\n\n2. **Added SAME_CUSTOMER error code** to src/errors.js\n\n3. **11 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - Basic merge: customer removed, invoices reassigned\n   - Error cases: CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND for missing customers, SAME_CUSTOMER for identical IDs\n   - ID normalization: handles mixed case and whitespace in parameters\n   - Immutability: original arrays unchanged after merge\n   - Edge cases: no invoices, many invoices from same customer, mixed case in invoice IDs\n   - Property preservation: all invoice properties maintained except customerId\n\nThe invoicing system now supports customer deduplication while maintaining full invoice history and audit trail!",
